Done. The root cause was a real bug: **`fn mci(...)` as a standalone statement was silently ignored** by the BASIC parser — only `let r = fn mci(...)` actually invoked the function. This meant:
- `close snd` never ran → aliases were never freed → MCIERR_DUPLICATE_ALIAS (289) on re-open
- Most demo files played nothing at all

Fixed by adding `Statement::Expr` so standalone `fn` calls execute for their side effects. Now you can `cargo run -- sound_demo.bas` yourself and hear all 4 sounds.

