dyncall itself has no knowledge of BASIC's `f64`-everything model. `read_field\<T\>` in `structs.rs` is strictly typed — you ask for `i32`, you get `i32`. The widening to `f64` happens in `read_struct_field_as_number` which is BASIC-specific code.

